## Target identity before materials

The reference target is not an undifferentiated “Dior Homme” impression. It is
the Dior Homme Intense re-edition sold in the 2011–2014 period and commonly
associated by collector photo chronology with formula code **05443/A**. A
reference sample must therefore be a documented 05443/A bottle with recorded
batch, acquisition, authenticity assessment, storage history, and opening date.
A bottle merely described as “2011” is not a sufficient target lock.

The target architecture supported across Dior and contemporaneous launch
material is:

- a short lavender veil;
- a dominant powdery iris/orris object;
- ambrette-mediated musk, pear-liqueur nuance, and silk-talc texture;
- restrained amber and vanilla warmth inside the iris fabric;
- a dry Virginia-cedar and vetiver return;
- an intimate musky-textile landing that retains iris rather than turning into
  laundry musk.

Velours d'Iris is an original architecture study using that silhouette. It is
not Dior's formula, a clone claim, a measured reconstruction, or evidence
of sensory similarity.

### Positive recognizers

1. Lavender is recognizable on fresh application but is no longer the subject
   by 30 minutes.
2. Iris/orris is the dominant named object at 5 minutes, 30 minutes, and 2
   hours, with powder body, violet movement, root coolness, and woody anatomy.
3. Pear is a small fermented or liqueur-like gleam *within* an ambrette/talc
   membrane, not a freestanding juicy-fruit note.
4. Warmth is perceived beneath the iris but cocoa, vanilla, tonka, and pastry
   are not named before iris.
5. Dry cedar and vetiver become clearer after the heart maximum while leaving a
   residual iris trace.
6. The 4-hour landing reads as dry wood, silk talc, warm fabric, and iris skin.

### Negative recognizers / immediate drift failures

- flat lipstick or chalky methyl-ionone wall;
- chocolate, brownie, praline, caramel, or pastry gourmand;
- leather, oud, or creamy sandalwood architecture associated with Dior Homme
  Parfum rather than DHI 05443/A;
- bright neroli-muguet soap or pressed-shirt Prada drift;
- cold blue Ambrox/amberwood pressure;
- syrupy pear candy;
- pencil shavings or hamster-bedding cedar;
- lavender-coumarin fougère;
- detergent white musk or anonymous musky persistence.

Complexity here means target-linked anatomy, perspective, texture, recurrence,
and temporal relation. Ingredient count earns no complexity credit.

## Evidence and uncertainty boundary

| Claim | Evidence class | Admitted use | Forbidden inference |
|---|---|---|---|
| Powdery Tuscan iris, Ecuadorian ambrette with pear-liqueur/silk-talc facets, Virginia cedar, amber, precious woods | persistent Dior house description | target identity and relation design | no 05443/A percentages or exact materials under `PARFUM` |
| Tuscan iris butter, ambrette seed absolute, Virginia cedar essence; woody fragrance warmed by iris and vanilla | Dior training material | corroborating iris/ambrette/cedar/vanillic architecture | no claim that the 2020 training page reveals a measured 2011 formula |
| Lavender; iris, ambrette, pear liqueur and powder; Virginia cedar and vetiver | contemporaneous 2011 launch report | 2011 phase and base recognizers | no laboratory or concentration authority |
| 05443/A associated with 2011–2014 | collector photo chronology | version lock, with moderate confidence | no Dior archival-formula authority |
| Community transcription lists alpha-isomethyl ionone, coumarin, benzyl benzoate | package-disclosure transcription | presence hypotheses only | ingredient order is not concentrate percentage |
| Cocoa/chocolate association | perfumer and wearer inference | a trace ablation question | cocoa is not a confirmed note or ingredient |
| Paid chromatographic reconstruction claims without public method and sample provenance | commercial analysis claim unverified | omission-hypothesis generation at most | no measured composition or exact-proportion claim |

No public analysis located in this review establishes all of: authenticated
05443/A bottle and batch, sample/storage provenance, chromatogram, peak table,
instrument method, retention/spectral evidence, reference standards,
calibration or response factors, co-elution treatment, and numerical
uncertainty. Exact molecular composition and proportions therefore remain
**UNKNOWN**.

Sources:

- [Dior product architecture](https://www.dior.com/en_ch/beauty/products/dior-homme-intense-Y0479201.html)
- [Dior 2020 fragrance training memo, page 82](https://www.diortraining.com/uploads/1/2/9/1/12917753/fragrance_memo_2020_english.pdf#page=82)
- [Contemporaneous 2011 launch report](https://www.fragrantica.com/news/Dior-Homme-2011-by-Francois-Demachy-Dior-Homme-Intense-2011-Francois-Demachy-Dior-J-adore-Eau-de-Toilette-2011-2383.html)
