## Phase architecture and transitions

| Phase / perspective | Foreground | Membrane or negative space | Rear / lower register | Required handoff | Collapse mode |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| opening, 0–5 min | fine lavender and linalyl softness | first talc haze around an emerging iris edge | transparent Iso E distance | herbal edges fold into powder | fougère, essential-oil blast, or instant lipstick block |
| full heart, 5–45 min | AIMI powder body with Alpha-Ionone movement | Ambrettolide proxy creates pear-liqueur/talc/skin continuity; Hedione ventilates edges | warm Tonkarome/Orivone shadow begins below | pear remains a glint inside iris | pear candy, wine musk, shampoo radiance, flat ionone wall |
| late heart, 45 min–2 h | iris remains named but gains root coolness | Cashmeran and slow Benzyl Benzoate form textile depth | cedar and vetiver become identifiable as a return | warmth stays underneath, wood moves forward | cocoa-tonka dessert or cosmetic musk plateau |
| drydown, 2–4 h+ | dry cedar-vetiver with residual iris | Ambrettolide/talc cloth closes toward skin | Benzyl Benzoate and Iso E sustain the rear plane | the initial powder recurs as a small skin memory | pencil wood, vetiver root subject, detergent musk, anonymous Iso E |

