| root specificity | Alpha Irone 10% | cool buttery rhizome accent | powder into lower warmth | generic synthetic iris | an expensive separate violet/orris object |
| warm orris seam | Orivone | fatty continuity between iris and amber | iris to warm shadow | a hard join | wax, butter, or extreme potency spike |
| ambrette membrane | Ambrettolide 10% | sole musk; pear/talc/skin mediation | all sides of iris and final skin closure | pear/talc disappears or detaches | wine musk, fruity musk, laundry musk |
| aromatic tailoring | Lavender EO and Linalyl Acetate | short cool entry and soft fold | opening into powder | no entry perspective | herbal oil or lavender-tonka fougère |
| amber warmth | Tonkarome | coumarinic temperature with a bounded vanillic facet | beneath iris and into wood | cold thin violet wood | almond hay, pastry, or overt tonka |
| roasted hypothesis | no Cocoa in the selected build; Cocoa Absolute is confined to 40/80 µL successor arms | test whether a roasted shadow is needed at all | warm shadow | selected zero-cocoa build proves sufficient | chocolate/brownie naming is target failure |
| Virginia cedar return | Cedarwood oil Virginia | dry named base marker | iris toward masculine late frame | cosmetic musk ending | pencil shavings or cedar subject |
| vetiver counterline | Vetiver EO (India) | earthy dry tension against powder | cedar return | cedar feels one-dimensional | smoke, root, green earth takeover |
| transparent rear chamber | Iso E Super | space and cedar-like extension | heart to drydown | hard iris/wood seam | generic woody aura |
| floral edge ventilation | Hedione | air around dense powder | opening and heart | opaque block | clean jasmine radiance dilutes identity |
| textile flex | Cashmeran | warm cloth between powder and wood | late heart into skin | brittle transition | plush spicy modern wood |
| slow fabric / replacement reservoir | Benzyl Benzoate | low-OAV mass, adhesion, and constant-total controls | lower heart and base | less slow continuity | excessive suppression or inert weight |

This ledger closes a computational design graph. It does not demonstrate that
the proposed relations occur in the bottle or resemble the reference.

## Dose geometry and takeover controls

- Nominal active iris system = **1,628 µL / 271,333.3333 ppm**: AIMI 1,140,
  Alpha Ionone 450, Alpha Irone 18 nominal, Orivone 20.
- Active iris system : nominal active Ambrettolide = **9.04 : 1**. That is a
  hierarchy statement, not a perceived-intensity equivalence.
- Lavender system = **220 µL / 36,666.6667 ppm**, bounded below the iris mass.
- Virginia cedar : vetiver = **300 : 240**, or **1.25 : 1** raw.
- Hedione + Iso E Super + Cashmeran + Benzyl Benzoate = **1,250 µL / 20.833%
  raw**, used as air, rear wood, textile flex, and slow fabric—not four named
  subjects.
- Warm-shadow active = **80 nominal µL / 13,333.3333 ppm** from Tonkarome.
- Cocoa Absolute is **0 µL in the selected build**. It has no right to enter
  except as a constant-total, constituent-composite OAV successor arm.
- Ambrettolide is the only musk: **180 nominal active µL / 30,000 ppm** from
  **1,800 µL raw 10% stock**. The direct 305 K formula-state screen raises it
  above modeled OAV 1, while the unresolved fraction basis and large DPG burden
  remain explicit limitations. No musk layering receives complexity credit.
- Every raw dose is at least 20 µL. No unprepared sub-10 µL raw dose is present.

## Material decisions and deliberate exclusions

| Candidate not used | Inventory / evidence state | Why excluded now | Missing effect, if any | Future controlled comparison |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Orris Liquid 30% w/w | owned; carrier unresolved | exact carrier displacement and active-volume authority unavailable | richer buttery naturalistic body | carrier-qualified one-for-one substitution inside the iris module |
| Ambrette seed absolute | TARGET / IDEAL, not in current live stock | current build uses Ambrettolide only as a declared proxy | natural seed complexity and literal house-note identity | replace proxy after lot and stock qualification, never call equivalent a priori |
| Dynascone or pear ester | owned candidate; not required | Dior describes ambrette itself between pear liqueur and talc; literal fruit risks syrup | possibly a brighter pear flash | first test Ambrettolide omission; add fruit only if pear recognizer is reliably absent |
| second musk | several owned alternatives | no distinct target-linked missing job; one Ambrettolide already owns mediation and closure | alternate diffusion only | one-for-one active-dose substitution, not additive stacking |
| Isobutyl Quinoline / Suederal | owned candidates | leather is not a supported hard 05443/A anchor and risks DHP drift | trace suede metaphor only | no test unless authenticated reference comparison reveals a stable leather defect |
| Ambrox Super / Ambrofix | owned or held stocks | risks modern cold amberwood pressure and current held-liquid authority issues | more force and persistence, not missing identity | none for V1 |
| Vanillin 10% | carrier unresolved | Tonkarome already supplies the bounded warm/vanillic facet | more literal vanilla | carrier-qualified substitution inside the warm-shadow module only |
| approximate Coumarin stock | about 25–30% in DPG | exact active dose cannot be preserved | direct coumarin material | exact prepared dilution versus Tonkarome after labeling and authority |
| Heliotropin | physical form/fraction unresolved | micro-volume and carrier accounting incomplete | almond-powder contour | prepare exact stock first, then substitute inside warm shadow |
| Isobutavan | available neat | the 20 µL draft was modeled below OAV 1 and its separate vanilla seam was redundant with Tonkarome | dry creamy warmth | substitute for equal active Tonkarome space only if the single-material warm shadow is deficient |
| Cocoa Absolute | available neat | the 20 µL draft was modeled below OAV 1; chocolate is an inference, not target truth, so zero is the selected dose | possible roasted darkness | 0/40/80 µL constant-total ablation with constituent-composite OAV |
| citrus bouquet | available | 2011 architecture centers lavender, not a citrus top | brightness | none unless the documented reference clearly demands it |
| depleted Tonalide, Macrolide, Musk Ketone | depleted and exception-only | unavailable, redundant, and target-unnecessary | none essential | no comparison authorized |

**Missing-chemical conclusion:** the largest gaps are an authenticated 05443/A
reference and qualified ambrette/orris materials, not more ingredients. The
current projection is sufficient to test the selected relational hypothesis.

## Controlled evidence plan

Every trial is made fresh as a versioned, immutable sample. Use the same ethanol lot,
raw-stock concentration, substrate, application mass, maturation,
room, and evaluation schedule. Use opaque codes, balanced presentation order,
at least one hidden repeated control, and fresh applications for each temporal
session to reduce adaptation and memory confounding. Record identity, target
fidelity, depth, richness, liking, projection, longevity, and defects as
separate endpoints.

### Probe 1 — complete architecture against reference

- Arms: coded Velours d'Iris; coded documented 05443/A reference; repeated
  Velours d'Iris control.
- Windows: 0 s, 5 min, 30 min, 2 h, 4 h.
- Promotion: only if the repeated control is reliable and the candidate shows
  dominant dimensional iris, relational pear/talc, lavender handoff, and
  cedar-vetiver return without a negative recognizer.
- Ceiling: can support observed sample-to-sample similarity for the tested lots
  only; cannot reveal Dior's formula.

### Probe 2 — Ambrettolide causal omission

- Selected: 1,800 µL of 10% Ambrettolide, 180 µL nominal active.
- Half: 900 µL Ambrettolide plus a basis-qualified carrier/structural
  replacement that preserves 6,000 µL total.
- Zero: carrier-match the entire selected stock contribution. Because the
  inventory says 10% in DPG but does not state fraction basis, a literal
  active/carrier split is not authorized until stock basis and density are
  documented.
- Endpoints: pear-liqueur nuance, silk talc, iris continuity, independent musk
  naming, skin recurrence, liking.

### Probe 3 — cocoa shadow ablation

- Selected zero: 0 Cocoa + 80 Benzyl Benzoate replacement space.
- Low: 40 Cocoa + 40 Benzyl Benzoate replacement space.
- High: 80 Cocoa + 0 Benzyl Benzoate replacement space.
- All arms retain the other 120 µL of Benzyl Benzoate and total 6,000 µL.
  Use the lowest nonzero dose only if zero is repeatably inferior on dark warmth
  and the addition is not worse on target fidelity. Reject literal cocoa if
  chocolate is named or zero is not inferior.

### Probe 4 — Orivone seam frontier

- 0 / 20 / 40 µL Orivone, inverse Benzyl Benzoate adjustment, 6,000 µL total.
- Select the lowest dose that repeatably improves the iris-to-warmth seam
  without butter or wax naming.

### Probe 5 — lavender frontier

- 100 / 140 / 180 µL Lavender EO, inverse Benzyl Benzoate adjustment.
- Select the lowest reliably recognizable opening dose that yields completely
  to iris by 30 minutes. A persistent lavender subject fails.

### Probe 6 — cedar-vetiver counterform

- 360:180, 300:240 selected, and 240:300 µL; cedar-plus-vetiver fixed at 540.
- Select the arm with a dry late return while neither pencil cedar nor earthy
  vetiver becomes a new subject.

### Probe 7 — iris anatomy versus ionone wall

- Selected four-part iris geometry.
- Equal nominal iris-active total collapsed toward AIMI.
- Selected geometry without Alpha Irone, with DEP carrier matched.
- Retain extra anatomy only if it produces repeatable root coolness, violet
  motion, and target fidelity without greater cosmetic flatness. Ingredient
  count alone cannot win.

## OAV, natural-mixture, and psychophysical policy

1. Lavender EO High Altitude, Vetiver EO (India), and Cedarwood oil Virginia
   use the repository's constituent-composite natural OAV. Any future Cocoa
   Absolute arm must do the same, never a monomolecular whole-material shortcut.
2. Every active dose above is convertible to active ppm under the declared
   repository volume convention. W/w stocks remain nominal active-volume
   proxies until density and basis permit exact mass conversion.
3. OAV = concentration ppm / ODT ppm for the declared phase and threshold
   basis. Headspace uses mole fraction, vapor pressure, and non-unit activity
   coefficient; an air ODT is not silently exchanged with an ethanol ODT.
4. OAV below 1 is acceptable for Benzyl Benzoate because its selected role is
   purely structural. A sub-threshold Ambrettolide, Alpha Irone, Orivone,
   lavender, cedar, vetiver, Tonkarome, or future Cocoa test row is a failure
   because its declared role requires perceptibility or causal testing.
5. Modeled OAV-per-time is a screening alarm, never percent perceived
   contribution, beauty, liking, or sensory-similarity evidence.
6. Separate formula materials can suppress, mask, or blend nonlinearly. The
   controlled probes, not ingredient arithmetic, decide whether a relation is
   present.

## Pre-release OAV headspace screen — direct state diagnostic, not a release gate

This screen was generated from the parser-visible formula with
`build_formula_state()` and `simulate_formula()` at **305 K**, skin context,
30.00 mL nominal finished volume, and the declared ethanol/water matrix. Its
headspace basis is `MODELED_FINISHED_PRODUCT_MATRIX_PROXY`; the temporal model
is `HEURISTIC_UNCALIBRATED`. Exact concentrate and finished-product ppm w/w are
unavailable because several densities and the Ambrettolide/Alpha-Irone/
Tonkarome carrier bases are unresolved. The values below are deterministic
model diagnostics, not measured headspace, percent perceived contribution,
reference similarity, or wear-life evidence.

**Model totals:** 6,000.0000 µL raw stock; 3,898.0000 µL nominal active
equivalent; 3,698.0000 µL modeled odorant active after the Benzyl Benzoate
structural classification; 1.570157672 total modeled vapor ppm at opening.

