The formula-state active-equivalent tier allocation is **T 2.1% / H 72.8% /
B 25.1%**. Despite the project reference describing this field as OAV-weighted,
the current implementation sums active µL by the engine's material-note label;
it must not be interpreted as a measured perceptual pyramid. The future-module
OAV-tier diagnostic separately reports approximately T 2% / H 97% / B 1%,
partly because the engine labels Iso E Super as heart while that module labels
it as base. That mismatch remains a data-quality flag rather than a reason to
rewrite the formula toward a generic 30:35:35 EdP target.

**Threshold result:** every selected character or transition material remains
at modeled OAV ≥ 1 at opening and at 4 h. Ambrettolide is deliberately the
narrowest functional margin: 1.156536 opening and 1.159420 at 4 h. Benzyl
Benzoate is 0.006886 opening and 0.006922 at 4 h; this is accepted only because
its selected job is structural mass/replacement space, not a perceptible note.

