### Perfumer analysis of the modeled screen

1. **Character** — The intended family is a dense iris/orris amber-wood with a
   short aromatic entry, a musk-fruit-talc membrane, restrained coumarinic
   warmth, and a cedar-vetiver return. It evokes the documented DHI 2011
   architecture without claiming Dior's formula. The computational structure
   is heart-dominant with a deliberately narrow top and a distinct dry counterform.

2. **Opening (0–5 min)** — Total modeled vapor is 1.570157672 ppm. Iso E is
   massive (>1000 OAV); Hedione, Lavender, Alpha Ionone, Orivone, and AIMI are
   very strong (100–1000); Linalyl Acetate is strong (50–100); Cashmeran and
   cedar are moderate (10–50); vetiver is perceptible (5–10); Alpha Irone,
   Tonkarome, and Ambrettolide are at threshold (1–5). This supports a highly
   legible aromatic/iris launch in the model, but the huge generic Iso E and
   Hedione OAVs are warnings against assuming the model predicts note naming.

3. **Heart (30 min–2 h)** — The screen keeps the iris anatomy, Iso E, Hedione,
   and lavender numerically active. The desired sensory event is not “all of
   these notes remain equally loud”; it is lavender adaptation and blending
   while ionone/orris and the ambrette membrane become the named object. Since
   the simulator does not model human adaptation or mixture masking, the
   lavender handoff is a required blind-test endpoint, not a computational pass.

4. **Drydown (2–4 h+)** — Formula-state base allocation rises only from 25.1%
   to 26.0%, while the engine still classifies Iso E as heart. At 4 h the
   cedar, vetiver, Tonkarome, Ambrettolide, and Alpha Irone rows all remain above
   OAV 1; therefore no declared base character is computationally dormant.
   The intended landing is dry cedar-vetiver, silk talc, and residual iris, but
   that character remains unobserved.

5. **Sillage & Diffusion** — Modeled opening diffusion is carried mainly by
   Lavender, Linalyl Acetate, Alpha Ionone, Iso E, and Hedione vapor. At 4 h,
   the highest modeled OAVs remain Iso E, Hedione, and the ionone system. The
   OAV-intelligence diffusion-layer check reports all layers present, but OAV
   is not a measured sillage radius and cannot establish projection.

6. **Longevity** — The simulator retains 5,754.094940 µL raw-equivalent at 4 h,
   a heuristic 4.098418% loss. That number is not calibrated to blotter or skin
   mass loss and cannot be converted into expected hours of wear. Longevity is
   `NOT TESTED` until a physical, mass-controlled wear study exists.

7. **Balance** — OAV contrast is computationally well spread:
   `sigma_log(OAV) = 1.07`, inside the generic 0.8–1.2 target. The same
   future-module diagnostic warns that Iso E and Hedione exceed generic
   woody-amber OAV bands, class distribution is incomplete, and its volatility
   balance is critical against a generic 30:35:35 EdP template. These are
   screening warnings, not target-fidelity failures; forcing DHI's narrow top
   into a generic pyramid would violate the name-first design rule.

8. **Flags** — Benzyl Benzoate is sub-threshold but structural; Ambrettolide is
   only just above threshold and its 10% stock basis is unspecified; numerous
   active masses use density fallbacks; natural OAVs are constituent-composite
   but not batch-specific; Iso E has a cross-module note-tier mismatch; the
   documented 05443/A comparison, IFRA/allergen review, stability, and physical
   performance are absent. Direct OAV intelligence has **zero blocking reasons**
   and status `WARN`, not release authority.

## Failure map and first isolated response

| Observation | Likely architectural cause | First isolated successor test | Forbidden inference |
|---|---|---|---|
| flat lipstick/chalk | too much undifferentiated AIMI or too little internal anatomy | iris-anatomy probe; do not add random materials | “more ingredients means more depth” |
| pear absent | Ambrettolide proxy insufficient or relation suppressed | Ambrettolide omission/half/selected comparison before adding fruit | “Dior must contain a large pear ester” |
| pear syrup | explicit or musky fruit too prominent | reduce causal fruit/musk variable only | “sweetness proves similarity” |
| lavender barbershop | opening dose or Tonkarome relation too strong | lavender frontier at constant total | “aromatic OAV proves the right opening” |
| chocolate dessert | literal cocoa not needed or warm shadow too high | zero-cocoa arm | “reviewer cocoa associations prove Cocoa Absolute” |
| cold and thin | warm shadow underbuilt | low/selected warm-shadow replacement test | “add more vanilla everywhere” |
| cedar pencil wall | cedar proportion too high or rear space too hard | cedar-vetiver frontier | “wood persistence proves target fit” |
| rooty/smoky base | vetiver stock or proportion too dominant | cedar-vetiver frontier with same lot | “natural complexity is automatically better” |
| detergent drydown | musk becomes an object | Ambrettolide omission and one-for-one alternative, never additive stack | “more musks improve luxury” |
| attractive but Prada-like | clean floral/soap relief displaced warm ambrette density | compare recognizers, not liking alone | “liked more means closer” |
| attractive but DHP-like | leather/oud/sandalwood became structural | remove the contaminating architecture | “same brand family is acceptable scope” |

## Promotion rules and authority receipt

| Authority | State | Requirement not yet met |
|---|---|---|
| 05443/A target architecture | `DESIGN READY` | model has evidence tiers, recognizers, forbidden drift, relations, and falsifiers |
| Candidate selection | `THEORY_SELECTED` | Ambrette-Orris Velvet Pareto-dominates the encoded alternatives; this is not sensory evidence |
| Current-inventory execution | `HOLD` | governed overlay is not bound to live inventory text |
| Exact active mass / finished ppm w/w | `HOLD` | w/w stock densities/bases and full matrix mass are incomplete |
| Headspace OAV | `MODELED SCREEN ONLY` | direct formula-state/simulator diagnostic exists below; full release preflight is authority-blocked |
| Observed identity / target fidelity | `NOT TESTED` | documented 05443/A blind comparison absent |
| Observed depth / richness | `NOT TESTED` | repeated assessor evidence absent |
| Observed liking / hedonism | `NOT TESTED` | separate blinded liking endpoint absent |
| Performance / longevity / sillage | `NOT TESTED` | no physical batch or wear data |
| Safety / IFRA / allergens / skin use | `HOLD` | current formula-specific safety assessment absent |
| Stability / compatibility | `NOT TESTED` | no physical batch, storage, or challenge evidence |
| Purchase / preparation / compounding | `FALSE` | this document grants no operational authority |
| Release | `FALSE` | architecture and software tests cannot release perfume |

Promotion is fail-closed. No overall score can override a failed version lock,
unreliable repeated control, negative recognizer, safety hold, or inventory
authority mismatch. Disagreement between assessors is retained rather than
averaged into fictitious consensus.

